/path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 32.49 -109.87)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="7.13" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.13)" width="5.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Thmproofx3.pic1.16" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">1</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 67.93 -109.87)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="7.13" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.13)" width="5.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Thmproofx3.pic1.17" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 103.36 -109.87)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="7.13" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.13)" width="5.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Thmproofx3.pic1.18" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 138.79 -109.87)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="7.13" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.13)" width="5.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Thmproofx3.pic1.19" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 174.22 -109.87)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="7.13" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.13)" width="5.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Thmproofx3.pic1.20" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 209.66 -109.87)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="7.13" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.13)" width="5.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Thmproofx3.pic1.21" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</span></div>
<p id="Thmproofx3.p3.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="Thmproofx3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Illustration with <math id="Thmproofx3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproofx3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=6</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
        
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We construct a request sequence <math id="Thmproofx3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> such that the <math id="Thmproofx3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th round subsequence equals <math id="Thmproofx3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{i^{\prime}}^{(1)},p_{i^{\prime}}^{(2)},\dots,p_{i^{\prime}}^{(\ell)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{i^{\prime}}^{(1)},p_{i^{\prime}}^{(2)},\dots,p_{i^{\prime}}^{(\ell)})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmproofx3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{\prime}=i\mod n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>mod</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{\prime}=i\mod n</annotation></semantics></math>. That is, the request repeats itself cyclically with a period of <math id="Thmproofx3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> rounds. We analyze the sequence in chunks of <math id="Thmproofx3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> rounds, meaning that within each such chunk, we observe <math id="Thmproofx3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\ell</annotation></semantics></math> total requests.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Since there are <math id="Thmproofx3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k+1</annotation></semantics></math> distinct pages, the <span id="Thmproofx3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LRU</span> policy will always evict a page just before it is needed again. This means that every request results in a cache miss. <span id="Thmproofx3.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Opt</span> evicts the last page requested at each cache miss, so suffers a cache miss every <math id="Thmproofx3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> requests.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, <math id="Thmproofx3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\CR(\textsc{LRU})\geqslant k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">C</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">LRU</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\CR(\textsc{LRU})\geqslant k</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Randomized Algorithms</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we turn our attention to randomized algorithms. Recall that in standard online paging, randomization can help improving the competitive ratio to <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{k}=\Theta(\log k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{k}=\Theta(\log k)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is tight, as discussed in Section <a href="#S1.SS2" title="1.2 Related Work ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Cache Management for Mixture-of-Experts LLMs – extended version" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>. The following theorem is the main result of this section, which establishes a lower bound on the competitive ratio for the layered paging problem.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.4</span></span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Every randomized algorithm for <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>-layered paging with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> experts has
competitive ratio at least <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max(H_{n},\frac{\log(\ell)}{6n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max(H_{n},\frac{\log(\ell)}{6n})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Before we present the proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4 ‣ 3.2 Randomized Algorithms ‣ 3 Competitive Analysis of Layered Paging ‣ Cache Management for Mixture-of-Experts LLMs – extended version" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, let us discuss its significance. First, note that layered paging becomes trivial from the point of view of competitive analysis if <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geqslant n\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geqslant n\ell</annotation></semantics></math>: this is because the algorithm can store all pages in the cache, and thus achieve a competitive ratio equal to 1. We can thus assume that <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leqslant n\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leqslant n\ell</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, if <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, then Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4 ‣ 3.2 Randomized Algorithms ‣ 3 Competitive Analysis of Layered Paging ‣ Cache Management for Mixture-of-Experts LLMs – extended version" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a> shows a lower bound <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(\log\ell)=\Omega(\log k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(\log\ell)=\Omega(\log k)</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, if <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, then the theorem shows a lower bound of <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(\log n)=\Omega(\log k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(\log n)=\Omega(\log k)</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the result shows that if either <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> is constant (as typically in practice), then any randomized algorithm has competitive ratio at least <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(\log k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(\log k)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is tight.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To prove Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4 ‣ 3.2 Randomized Algorithms ‣ 3 Competitive Analysis of Layered Paging ‣ Cache Management for Mixture-of-Experts LLMs – extended version" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, we will rely on a variant of the coupon collector problem known as the <span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">parallel</span> coupon collector problem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>. In this problem, there are <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> different types of coupons, and <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> agents (collectors). In each round, each of the <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> agents selects one of the <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> coupon types uniformly at random. Agents are not allowed to exchange or share their coupons. Define <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(N,C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(N,C)</annotation></semantics></math> as the number of rounds after which each agent has collected all <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> coupons. Note that this problem is a generalization of the well-known vanilla coupon collector problem in which <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=1</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>, which is a key part in the analysis of the standard online paging problem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>. We are interested in bounding from below the <span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">cover time</span>, namely the quantity <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))</annotation></semantics></math>. We accomplish this in the following theorem, as previous work did not establish usable bounds <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.5</span></span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the parallel coupon collector with <math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math> coupons and <math id="S3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> agents, its cover time is such that</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))\geqslant\max\{N\cdot H_{N},\frac{\log C}{6}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))\geqslant\max\{N\cdot H_{N},\frac{\log C}{6}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproofx4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmproofx4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We prove the lower bounds separately, starting by <math id="Thmproofx4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))\geqslant N\cdot H_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))\geqslant N\cdot H_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We focus of the first collector, corresponding to the first layer. We know from the traditional
coupon collector problem that it will finish on average after <math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="NH_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">NH_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>
rounds. By definition,
all the collectors finish collecting their coupons after the first collector finishes its
collection, hence the first bound:
<math id="Thmproofx4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))\geqslant\mathbb{E}(T(N,1))=NH_{N}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))\geqslant\mathbb{E}(T(N,1))=NH_{N}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We now show that <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))\geqslant\frac{\log(C)}{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))\geqslant\frac{\log(C)}{6}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmproofx4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We first compute the probability of the expected time to complete
all collections to be larger than <math id="Thmproofx4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. By definition:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(T(N,C)\geqslant t)=1-\mathbb{P}(T(N,C)&lt;t)=1-\prod_{i=1}^{\ell}\mathbb{P}(T(N,1)&lt;t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(T(N,C)\geqslant t)=1-\mathbb{P}(T(N,C)&lt;t)=1-\prod_{i=1}^{\ell}\mathbb{P}(T(N,1)&lt;t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproofx4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Considering only the probability of not getting the first coupon, we get:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(T(N,C)\geqslant t)\geqslant 1-\left(1-\left(\frac{N-1}{N}\right)^{t}\right)^{C}\geqslant 1-\exp(-C\p*{\frac{N-1}{N}}^t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(T(N,C)\geqslant t)\geqslant 1-\left(1-\left(\frac{N-1}{N}\right)^{t}\right)^{C}\geqslant 1-\exp(-C\p*{\frac{N-1}{N}}^t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproofx4.p4.3" class="ltx_p">For <math id="Thmproofx4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t={\log(\frac{C}{\log(2)})}\penalty\ /\penalty\ {\log(\frac{N}{N-1})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t={\log(\frac{C}{\log(2)})}\penalty\ /\penalty\ {\log(\frac{N}{N-1})}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="Thmproofx4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(T\big(N,C)\geqslant t\big)\geqslant\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(T\big(N,C)\geqslant t\big)\geqslant\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Thus <math id="Thmproofx4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))\geqslant{\log(\frac{C}{\log(2)})}\penalty\ /\penalty\ {2\log(\frac{N}{N-1})}\geqslant\frac{\log(C)}{6}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn> 2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))\geqslant{\log(\frac{C}{\log(2)})}\penalty\ /\penalty\ {2\log(\frac{N}{N-1})}\geqslant\frac{\log(C)}{6}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">With more details: Using <math id="Thmproofx4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\log(\frac{N}{N-1})=\log(\frac{C}{\log(2)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\log(\frac{N}{N-1})=\log(\frac{C}{\log(2)})</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="S3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle t\log(\frac{N-1}{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle t\log(\frac{N-1}{N})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log(\frac{\log(2)}{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log(\frac{\log(2)}{C})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\frac{N-1}{N}\right)^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\frac{N-1}{N}\right)^{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\log(2)}{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\log(2)}{C}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-C\left(\frac{N-1}{N}\right)^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-C\left(\frac{N-1}{N}\right)^{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log(\frac{1}{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log(\frac{1}{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp(-C \p*{\frac{N-1}{N}}^t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp(-C \p*{\frac{N-1}{N}}^t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1-\exp(-C \p*{\frac{N-1}{N}}^t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1-\exp(-C \p*{\frac{N-1}{N}}^t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody><tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left" style="white-space:normal;" colspan="5">Thus:</td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(T(N,C)\geqslant\frac{\log(\frac{C}{\log(2)})}{\log(\frac{N}{N-1})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(T(N,C)\geqslant\frac{\log(\frac{C}{\log(2)})}{\log(\frac{N}{N-1})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geqslant\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩾</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geqslant\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geqslant\frac{\log(\frac{C}{\log(2)})}{2\log(\frac{N}{N1})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩾</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geqslant\frac{\log(\frac{C}{\log(2)})}{2\log(\frac{N}{N1})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geqslant\frac{\log(\frac{C}{\log(2)})}{2(1+\frac{N}{N-1})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩾</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geqslant\frac{\log(\frac{C}{\log(2)})}{2(1+\frac{N}{N-1})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geqslant\frac{N-1}{4N-2}\log(\frac{C}{\log(2)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geqslant\frac{N-1}{4N-2}\log(\frac{C}{\log(2)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geqslant\frac{1}{6}\log(\frac{C}{\log(2)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geqslant\frac{1}{6}\log(\frac{C}{\log(2)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}(T(N,C))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geqslant\frac{\log(C)}{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩾</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geqslant\frac{\log(C)}{6}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproofx4.p6.2" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We can now proceed with the proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4 ‣ 3.2 Randomized Algorithms ‣ 3 Competitive Analysis of Layered Paging ‣ Cache Management for Mixture-of-Experts LLMs – extended version" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>. It relies on showing that every randomized paging algorithm has a competitive ratio at least <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\ell}{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}(T(n,\ell))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\ell}{k}\cdot\mathbb{E}(T(n,\ell))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproofx5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof</span></span><span id="Thmproofx5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4 ‣ 3.2 Randomized Algorithms ‣ 3 Competitive Analysis of Layered Paging ‣ Cache Management for Mixture-of-Experts LLMs – extended version" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproofx5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider an instance of the layered paging problem such that <math id="Thmproofx5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\ell=k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\ell=k+1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="Thmproofx5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> be a randomized algorithm. Using Yao’s principle, we consider a
random sequence <math id="Thmproofx5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> as input, such that the <math id="Thmproofx5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th requested page <math id="Thmproofx5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is drawn uniformly at random
among the <math id="Thmproofx5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> pages of layer <math id="Thmproofx5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\mod\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>mod</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\mod\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="Thmproofx5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is considered
deterministic.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">At the start of a round, the deterministic algorithm has all pages but one in cache.
There is at least a <math id="Thmproofx5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}</annotation></semantics></math> chance of having a cache miss per
round, the probability of drawing the missing page. There are <math id="Thmproofx5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{|\sigma|}{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{|\sigma|}{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> rounds, thus we have:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}(A(\sigma))\geqslant\frac{|\sigma|}{\ell n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}(A(\sigma))\geqslant\frac{|\sigma|}{\ell n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For the analysis of the optimal algorithm <span id="Thmproofx5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Opt</span>, we partition the random
sequence <math id="Thmproofx5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> into blocks such that each block is a minimal contiguous sub-sequence containing <math id="Thmproofx5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k+1</annotation></semantics></math>
distinct elements. <span id="Thmproofx5.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Opt</span> must suffer at least one cache miss per block, as its cache is missing one requested page at the start of each block.
It remains to estimate the size of the blocks. There is an equivalence with the parallel coupon collector problem, with <math id="Thmproofx5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>
coupons and <math id="Thmproofx5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> collectors, associating a round of <math id="Thmproofx5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> requests to
one parallel step of all collectors. The average length of a block is then <math id="Thmproofx5.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}(T(n,\ell))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}(T(n,\ell))</annotation></semantics></math> rounds of <math id="Thmproofx5.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> requests.
For a sequence <math id="Thmproofx5.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> long enough compared to <math id="Thmproofx5.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproofx5.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, we can estimate the number of blocks in the sequence to the inverse of the average length of a block times the length of the sequence. We therefore obtain <math id="Thmproofx5.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}(\textsc{Opt}(\sigma))\leqslant\frac{|\sigma|}{\ell\mathbb{E}(T(n,\ell))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Opt</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}(\textsc{Opt}(\sigma))\leqslant\frac{|\sigma|}{\ell\mathbb{E}(T(n,\ell))}</annotation></semantics></math>. We conclude:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}(A(\sigma))\geqslant\frac{|\sigma|}{\ell n}\geqslant\mathbb{E}(\textsc{Opt}(\sigma))\frac{\ell\mathbb{E}(T(n,\ell))}{\ell n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Opt</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}(A(\sigma))\geqslant\frac{|\sigma|}{\ell n}\geqslant\mathbb{E}(\textsc{Opt}(\sigma))\frac{\ell\mathbb{E}(T(n,\ell))}{\ell n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx5.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Thus <math id="Thmproofx5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\CR(A)\geqslant\frac{\mathbb{E}(T(n,\ell))}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">C</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\CR(A)\geqslant\frac{\mathbb{E}(T(n,\ell))}{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, for a long enough <math id="Thmproofx5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx5.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4 ‣ 3.2 Randomized Algorithms ‣ 3 Competitive Analysis of Layered Paging ‣ Cache Management for Mixture-of-Experts LLMs – extended version" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a> then follows from Theorem <a href="#S3.Ex5" title="Theorem 3.5 ‣ 3.2 Randomized Algorithms ‣ 3 Competitive Analysis of Layered Paging ‣ Cache Management for Mixture-of-Experts LLMs – extended version" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a> :</p>
<table id="S3.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\CR(A)\geqslant\frac{\mathbb{E}(T(n,\ell))}{n}\geqslant\max\left(H_{n},\frac{\log(\ell)}{6n}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">C</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>⩾</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\CR(A)\geqslant\frac{\mathbb{E}(T(n,\ell))}{n}\geqslant\max\left(H_{n},\frac{\log(\ell)}{6n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproofx5.p7.2" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Contrarily to the classical paging problem, it is still an open question
whether there exist randomized algorithms reaching this ratio, or simply
with a better competitive ratio that <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>A Layered Extension of the <span id="S4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LRU</span> Algorithm</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we propose an extension of the <span id="S4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LRU</span> algorithm adapted to the problem at hand. The algorithm handles better some pathological scenarios specific to this problem. More specifically, note that the standard <span id="S4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LRU</span> policy evicts the oldest page in the cache, regardless of which
layer it belongs to. This is intuitively inefficient: if a page of layer <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is currently served, then it is generally unsafe to evict a page belonging to layer <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i+1</annotation></semantics></math>, since it may be requested in the immediately following step. Instead, a more reasonable choice is to evict a page of layer <math id="S4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i-1</annotation></semantics></math> or even <math id="S4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. We thus seek a <span id="S4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">layer-specific</span> variant of <span id="S4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LRU</span>, and to this end we define two quantities, specific to a page <math id="S4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> in cache and a time <math id="S4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a page <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> in the cache at the current time <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(p,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(p,t)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the last time that <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> was requested. We define the <span id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">last-round index</span> of <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(p,t)=\lfloor\frac{t-\tau(p,t)}{\ell}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(p,t)=\lfloor\frac{t-\tau(p,t)}{\ell}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>, as the number of rounds between
<math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(p,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(p,t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. We also define the <span id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">relative layer distance of <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math></span>, noted <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(p,t)=\tau(p,t)-t\mod\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>mod</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(p,t)=\tau(p,t)-t\mod\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, as the number of requests needed before reaching the layer in which <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> belongs.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Using the above definitions, we define the <span id="S4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Layered Last Recently Used</span> caching algorithm (<span id="S4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LLRU</span>), as the policy which, on a cache miss at time <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, evicts the page <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> with largest index <math id="S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(p,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(p,t)</annotation></semantics></math>, and in the event of ties evicts the page with largest index <math id="S4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(p,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(p,t)</annotation></semantics></math>. This allows, intuitively, to evict pages which have not been requested since a large number of rounds, and whose layer will be requested the latest. Figure <a href="#S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 4 A Layered Extension of the LRU Algorithm ‣ Cache Management for Mixture-of-Experts LLMs – extended version" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> illustrates an execution of <span id="S4.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LLRU</span>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
